TA-zfspool
====

Collects storage-pool integrity from whatever is present: ZFS (zpool status/get), Linux md RAID (/proc/mdstat + mdadm --detail) and btrfs (filesystem usage + device stats). Emits per-pool state (degraded, sync/rescan progress, reserved space, uncorrectable errors) as JSON events to index=main (sourcetype zfspool:status) and numeric zfspool.* metrics to index=metrics (sourcetype zfspool:metrics), with overview and metrics dashboards.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * At least one of: zfs-utils, mdadm, btrfs-progs (the collector auto-detects and skips absent subsystems)
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="zfspool:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="zfspool:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="zfspool.*" by host
  | mstats avg("zfspool.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=zfspool:status  (per-pool JSON: subsystem, state, degraded flag,
recovery %, vdev counts; alarm status when any pool is degraded/off)
Metrics: zfspool.<subsystem>_<pool>_<attribute> on index=metrics
Dashboards: TA-Zfspool > Zfspool Overview / Zfspool Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-zfspool/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * A healthy host with no pools still emits an 'absent' status event so reporting is visible.
  * md details require mdadm to be installed; without it only /proc/mdstat is parsed.
  * zpool scrub/rescan progress is only non-zero while a scrub is running.

License
-------
SOURCE-AVAILABLE (see LICENSE) - free personal, educational and evaluation
use; commercial or production use requires a paid license from BentleyPC
LLC (https://www.bentleypc.com/TA-zfspool).

Enter your key (format BP-...) after purchase using EITHER method:

  1. Splunk Web: open the app, click "License" in the nav, click a row to
     open the key entry page, paste the key and Save.

  2. File (headless / forwarder friendly): create the file
     $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-zfspool/local/license.conf with:

         [settings]
         telemetry_enabled = 1
         key = BP-xxxxxxxxxxxx

     No restart required - the hourly beacon reads this file on every run.

Set telemetry_enabled = 0 to keep the key for validation but pause all
outbound beacons. The beacon sends only: license key, hostname, app name
and app version to the BentleyPC license API (see api_base in
default/license.conf). It is telemetry only - never a license check that
blocks functionality.
